# CORV GCS — boat SITL (ArduRover on the 'motorboat' model)
# A survey boat on Lake Garda: boat frame, at most 2 m/s on the lanes, and the
# afternoon "Ora" — a southerly breeze of 5 m/s — with the short chop it raises
# over the southern basin. SITL's own wave model moves the hull (roll, pitch,
# heave), so the attitude in the telemetry and the true pose the rosbridge
# emulator ray-casts its sonar from see the same sea.

FRAME_CLASS     2

# --- RC calibration ---
RC1_MIN 1000
RC1_MAX 2000
RC1_TRIM 1500
RC2_MIN 1000
RC2_MAX 2000
RC2_TRIM 1500
RC3_MIN 1000
RC3_MAX 2000
RC3_TRIM 1500
RC4_MIN 1000
RC4_MAX 2000
RC4_TRIM 1500

# --- small INS offsets so the IMU counts as calibrated ---
INS_ACCOFFS_X   0.001
INS_ACCOFFS_Y   0.001
INS_ACCOFFS_Z   0.001
INS_ACCSCAL_X   1.001
INS_ACCSCAL_Y   1.001
INS_ACCSCAL_Z   1.001
COMPASS_OFS_X   5
COMPASS_OFS_Y   13
COMPASS_OFS_Z   -18

# --- survey speed and lane following: a sonar survey boat, 2 m/s at most ---
CRUISE_SPEED    2
WP_SPEED        2
WP_RADIUS       3
WP_OVERSHOOT    2

# --- the lake: a southerly 5 m/s, waves 0.5 m high, 12 m long, at the
# deep-water speed for that length (sqrt(g λ / 2π) ≈ 4.3 m/s) ---
# SITL's boat (SIM_Sailboat.cpp, which MotorBoat reuses) only makes waves
# once armed, takes half of SIM_WAVE_AMP as the amplitude (slopes up to ~7°
# here) and heaves only with SIM_WAVE_ENABLE 2.
SIM_WIND_SPD    5
SIM_WIND_DIR    180
SIM_WIND_TURB   1
SIM_WAVE_ENABLE 2
SIM_WAVE_AMP    0.5
SIM_WAVE_LENGTH 12
SIM_WAVE_DIR    180
SIM_WAVE_SPEED  4.3
